    "final_text": "I fixed all five bugs in `src/cart.js` and added regression tests. All 79 tests pass (`npm test`, exit code 0) and `npm run lint` is clean. The work is on branch `fix/shopping-cart-bugs`, and the first commit is the original code exactly as given, so the fix shows up as a diff.\n\n| # | Bug | Fix |\n|---|-----|-----|\n| 1 | `addItem` accepted a negative price or quantity | Price must be a number \u2265 0 (free items are allowed); quantity must be a whole number of at least 1. Checks run before anything changes, including when adding more of an existing item. |\n| 2 | `removeItem` used `=`, which renamed every item and removed nothing | Matches with `===`. Returns `true` if it removed the item, `false` if the item wasn't in the cart. |\n| 3 | `getTotal` loop used `<=`, so it crashed on every call, even for an empty cart | Sums with `reduce`. |\n| 4 | Discount was added to the total | Now subtracted. |\n| 5 | `applyDiscount` accepted any value | Only 0\u2013100 is accepted; a rejected value keeps the previous discount. |\n\n**Tests:**\n- **`tests/cart.test.js`** has tests for each method plus a `regressions` block with tests named `bug 1:` through `bug 5:`. All ten fail against the original code.\n- **Checking each test on its own:** bug 3 crashes `getTotal`, so running against the original can't show that the bug 4 test works independently. I put each bug back, one at a time, into a copy of the fixed file. Each copy failed its own bug's tests. The bug 3 copy also failed the bug 4 test, because that test calls `getTotal`.\n- **Two extra test files:** `tests/cart.edge.test.js` covers unicode names, number limits, odd input types and large carts. `tests/cart.integration.test.js` covers multi-step flows and checks that separate carts don't share state.\n- **Lint:** I added ESLint with a rule that flags the `i.name = name` mistake from bug 2 in the original code.\n\n**A sixth problem the edge tests found:** a new item accepted a quantity above JavaScript's largest safe integer, while adding to an existing item rejected it. Both now reject it.\n\n**Choices I made where the task didn't say:**\n- Adding a name that's already in the cart keeps the first price. That was the original behaviour.\n- Names must match exactly, including case and spaces.\n- The total isn't rounded to cents, because not every currency uses two decimals. Round when displaying it.\n- `getItemCount` still counts distinct items, not total quantity.\n\nThe README lists all the fixes and choices. There's no git remote, so nothing was pushed.",
